        <exercise id="_0d296047-b708-4c1c-8209-485a90347764" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para>When the price is \($50\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! There are 0 tickets sold when the price is $50 per ticket.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 0. There are 0 tickets sold when the price is $50 per ticket.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_78e21919-1cfc-40c4-a162-1501451e63af" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> When the price is \(p\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(392p\)</para>
            <para>\(400-8p\)</para>
            <para>\(p(400-8p)\)</para>
            <para>\(p(8p-400)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para> Correct! \(400-8p\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(400-8p\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_211a0bc1-f3d7-46be-ba7b-7459987ab296" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para>Answer questions a-g to complete the right column in the table to find out what revenues the theater expects to receive at the given ticket prices.</para>
            <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
              <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Ticket price (dollars)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Number of tickets sold</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Revenue (dollars)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(5\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(360\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(1800\)</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(10\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>a. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(15\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>b. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(20\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>c. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(30\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>d. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(45\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>e. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(50\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>f. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>\(p\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>g. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
            <para>When the price is \($10\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The revenue is $3,200 when the price is $10 per ticket.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 3,200. The revenue is $3,200 when the price is $10 per ticket.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d9e377f9-6f95-44c7-96c0-f454c98ba6f1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para>When the price is \($15\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The revenue is $4,200 when the price is $15 per ticket.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 4,200. The revenue is $4,200 when the price is $15 per ticket.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_598a1efc-a029-4f43-b294-826ffd40dd2c" class="multiple-choice">
